{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1002887-horror-action-themed-scenario-or-plot-seed","id":1002887,"title":"Horror/Action Themed Scenario or Plot Seed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T07:59:17-08:00","id":1002887,"title":"Horror/Action Themed Scenario or Plot Seed","content":"Having just seen Dr. Strange I'd like to run a MtA 2e 1 shot for my son and friends for his birthday! Can anyone recommend an existing scenario from 1e or something else that would let me crank out a good action-oriented 1-shot (hopefully I can seduce him away from savage worlds and dungeon crawl classics :-) ). Thanks!<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone have a 1-sheet sort of reference thing (there were a ton of these produced for 1e) of tight rule summaries for 2e Mage (or even CoD core)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:14:36-08:00","id":1003057,"title":"","content":"I don't know how old your son is, but Mage doesn't really do &quot;Action&quot; good. Mostly because single spell can halt all action and resolve most of action-y conflicts. Action related conflict resolutions are pretty overshadowed by superior alternatives.<br /> <br /> Still, it can work as long as players don't reach for these superior options. I liked that A-something Cipher adventure for 1e; it has potential for action segment with the whole hostage situation thing. Just make sure to spice it up a little by adding demons, monsters or other stuff to &quot;just&quot; grunts. Maybe make the artifact in question release something actiony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:21:53-08:00","id":1003063,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with a one round action sequence, and its brevity doesn't prevent it from being action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:58:26-08:00","id":1003086,"title":"","content":"We had an interesting fight that had Cold Snap and Deepen Shadows both enhanced with Reach doom the battlefield, a large and cluttered house, into a treacherous mess.<br /> <br /> One of the SAS's for Mage involved, I think, mages taking people hostage at a museum, including the players. You might look to the various <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Storytelling_Adventure_System\" target=\"_blank\">SAS's </a>if you want a prepared adventure. There's a book called Reign of the Exarchs that has five longish stories, I believe some of them can fall into action scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:08:06-08:00","id":1003092,"title":"","content":"In Lines of Power there's basically a one-shot you could adapt to 2e that involves some opportunistic assholes planting a mole and then breaking into the PCs sanctum to take control of the Hallow and do morally questionable experiments on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:27:16-08:00","id":1003127,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the great advice! Has something changed in 2e? When we played 1e up through 3 dots in Arcanum we had lots of action. Is it because we didn't do a lot of improvised magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:57:05-08:00","id":1003141,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's always been like that, you usually just need one clever spell to get around any particular obstacle. For instance, I once ended an Astral bar fight by using Matter 2 to drop everyone's pants and make them trip and fall down. If your group hasn't been improvising then that could be part of why you've had longer action sequences than not. If you think about it though, even in an action movie, the actual action is frequently punctuated with a single high tension act. The samurai duel that ends with both opponents striking and one falling dead, the hidden gun or knife that comes out and gives one side the sudden advantage, etc. That's the kind of action that Mage can frequently boil down to. Sometimes it's not easy to think of the easiest, best way to drop a foe, or you really want to drag a beat down out because you like shape shifting or whatever, Mage handles that kind of action just as well, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}